<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Belgrade (1521)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1521</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungarian-wars">Ottoman–Hungarian wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in 1521 was the capture of the Hungarian fortress city by the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a>. It opened the way for the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, which culminated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Battle of Mohács</a> in 1526. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> profile places it among Suleiman's major campaigns.</p></div>
